---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Homelab Disaster Recovery Platform"
  description="A practical disaster recovery framework using Restic backups, automation, monitoring and recovery validation."
>

<section class="project-hero">
  <div class="container project-hero-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Infrastructure Resilience Case Study</p>

      <h1>Disaster recovery designed for rebuild, not just backup.</h1>

      <p class="project-summary">
        A practical recovery platform using Restic backups, automation,
        monitoring and validation procedures to restore homelab services after
        hardware or system failure.
      </p>

      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button button-primary"
          href="/projects">
          Back to projects
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="project-facts">
      <p class="eyebrow">Project Overview</p>

      <dl>
        <div><dt>Platform</dt><dd>Linux Homelab</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Backup Engine</dt><dd>Restic</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Validation</dt><dd>Recovery testing</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Monitoring</dt><dd>Prometheus / Grafana</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Status</dt><dd class="live-status">Active project</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="section">
<div class="container content-grid">

<div class="section-heading">
<p class="eyebrow">The Challenge</p>
<h2>Backups are only useful when recovery is proven.</h2>
</div>

<div class="prose">
<p>
The platform provides automated backups of critical infrastructure,
configuration and application data, but the primary objective is recovery
confidence.
</p>

<p>
The disaster recovery process documents how services can be rebuilt onto
replacement hardware, including Raspberry Pi recovery scenarios.
</p>
</div>

</div>
</section>


<section class="section section-soft">
<div class="container">

<div class="section-heading">
<p class="eyebrow">Recovery Workflow</p>
<h2>Backup through to validated restoration.</h2>
</div>

<div class="architecture">

<div class="architecture-item">
<span>01</span>
<strong>Backup</strong>
<p>Restic snapshots protect system and application data.</p>
</div>

<div class="architecture-item">
<span>02</span>
<strong>Monitor</strong>
<p>Prometheus metrics track backup health and age.</p>
</div>

<div class="architecture-item">
<span>03</span>
<strong>Rebuild</strong>
<p>Replacement hardware is prepared and restored.</p>
</div>

<div class="architecture-item">
<span>04</span>
<strong>Validate</strong>
<p>Services are tested before returning to production.</p>
</div>

</div>

</div>
</section>


<section class="section">
<div class="container">

<div class="grid capability-grid">

<article class="card">
<h3>Restic backups</h3>
<p>
Encrypted repositories with retention policies and automated execution.
</p>
</article>

<article class="card">
<h3>Recovery testing</h3>
<p>
A planned DR exercise using replacement hardware to prove rebuild capability.
</p>
</article>

<article class="card">
<h3>Observability</h3>
<p>
Backup success, age and storage health exposed through monitoring.
</p>
</article>

<article class="card">
<h3>Infrastructure recovery</h3>
<p>
Documented restoration of Linux hosts, Docker workloads and services.
</p>
</article>

</div>

</div>
</section>


</BaseLayout>
